{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 2 RCA + implementation — disposition-preserving fallback chain (supersedes C.c1)\n\nThe operator redirected away from the earlier broad \"C.c1\" (`should_fall_back` WAIT_AND_RETRY-exclusion) to a **disposition-preserving fallback chain**. The C.c1 edits were fully reverted; scope is now **3 files** (failure.py, model_classes.py, the new oracle) because the primary predicate contract is UNCHANGED.\n\n### Re-confirmed root-cause chain (against the code)\n1. `bedrock:opus` throttled → botocore adaptive retry exhausts → `ModelHTTPError(429)` → `WAIT_AND_RETRY` (retryable).\n2. `should_fall_back(429)`=True → chain moves to `anthropic:opus`.\n3. Fallback keyless → instant `TypeError: Could not resolve authentication method`; `should_fall_back(TypeError)`=False. Read `pydantic_ai/models/fallback.py`: on a leg whose `fallback_on` is False the loop **bare-reraises that leg's exception alone** and never builds the `FallbackExceptionGroup` — so the primary's retained retryable 429 is DISCARDED.\n4. `classify_llm_failure(TypeError)` → `NEEDS_INVESTIGATION` → hard **INDETERMINATE** (not exit-11). Shared Bedrock account ⇒ fleet-wide simultaneity.\n5. LATENT SECOND BUG: even if a group WERE produced, `failure._map` classified `FallbackExceptionGroup` with a blanket `CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL`, ignoring the leg dispositions — the retryable primary would still be masked.\n\n### The two changes (both at the shared classification/construction core)\n**Change 1 — `model_classes.py` (retain-the-group, leg-aware).** `should_fall_back` now returns True immediately for any exception tagged as a NON-PRIMARY leg failure (`_FALLBACK_LEG_ATTR`), so the chain EXHAUSTS INTO a `FallbackExceptionGroup` bundling every leg (including the primary's retained 429) rather than bare-reraising the terminal leg. Non-primary candidates are tagged by a tiny `_wrap_fallback_leg` `WrapperModel` applied in `build_fallback_model` (primary at index 0 is NOT wrapped). The primary keeps the deliberately NARROW guard verbatim — a credential/size/quota error still fails LOUD and is never masked by shopping for a working key. A stateful call-counter was rejected (unsafe under concurrency/streaming); an always-True predicate was rejected (a fallback SUCCESS would then mask a primary credential error); a denylist predicate was rejected (broadens PRIMARY failover). Leg-awareness is the minimal seam that satisfies \"retain the group at the last leg\" AND \"preserve the narrow primary guard\".\n\n**Change 2 — `failure.py` (classify a group by its MOST-RECOVERABLE leg).** The `_map` group arm now calls `_classify_fallback_group`, which classifies each leg through the TOTAL public classifier and returns the most-recoverable (`WAIT_AND_RETRY`/`RETRY_NOW` on ANY leg wins). An all-non-retryable group keeps `CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL`. `_RETRYABLE` unchanged. Net: throttle → group [429, TypeError] → `WAIT_AND_RETRY` → **exit-11 retryable**.\n\n### RED → GREEN\nHeld-out oracle `tests/unit/test_throttle_no_failover_1c0d.py` (4 tests). Confirmed RED on pre-fix source (via `git stash` of only the source files): the e2e produced the exact incident signature (`TypeError: Could not resolve authentication method` → `NEEDS_INVESTIGATION` → retryable=False), and the group-classifier test failed on the blanket arm. GREEN post-fix: `58 passed` (4 oracle + the pre-existing `test_llm_fallback_chain.py` + `test_llm_failure_classifier.py` suites, unchanged and still GREEN — proving the primary contract is preserved).\n\n### Mutation-with-teeth (inside `sandbox-exec -f`, no `timeout` binary on host)\n- (a) revert Change 2 to blanket `CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL` → group test RED. ✓ killed.\n- (b) revert Change 1 so the chain bare-reraises → e2e RED reproducing the exact keyless-auth INDETERMINATE. ✓ killed.\nRestored byte-identical → GREEN. Sandbox verified to deny `$HOME` writes / allow `$PWD`.\n\n### Surface-parity census — PASS (one fix, all surfaces)\nBoth changes live at shared cores, inherited once by review-plan / verify-completion / review-code / claim / close (all run through `PydanticAIRunner.run`):\n- Change 2 (`classify_llm_failure`) is reached through the ONE mid-run seam `run_failure.interpret_failure` (`run_failure.py:165`, called from `runner.py:667`) plus the preflight seam `runner.py:337`. Other callers are only the internal recursion in `_classify_fallback_group` and `should_fall_back`.\n- Change 1 (`build_fallback_model`/`should_fall_back`) is reached through the ONE construction site `runner.py:467`.\nNo per-surface duplication; no out-of-scope slot. `failure.py:351` confirms retryable (WAIT_AND_RETRY/RETRY_NOW) drives exit 11; everything else INDETERMINATE — so the group→WAIT_AND_RETRY classification surfaces as exit-11 end-to-end.\n\n### Refactoring litmus + fix-safety audit\nRestoration/addition, not test-weakening: tests assert only the observable disposition/exit (`classify_llm_failure(...).retryable`/`resolution_class`), never internal structure. No new dependency (WrapperModel is already a pydantic-ai dependency, mirrored from `tracing._TracedCandidateModel`). No existing test relaxed — the preserved suites pass unedited. `make lint` (incl. module-size + complexity ratchet) and `make typecheck` (692 files) clean; both files under the 800 LOC cap (failure.py 720, model_classes.py 680).\n\n### Attribution\ncaused_by `8fbd-e9d5-326e-40d8` (commit `6d4f394195b2`, \"Enable class-scoped Anthropic fallback\", 2026-08-10), class `plan_defect`. git-blame + date-test: the leg-agnostic `should_fall_back` (`72e59d982fee`, 2026-07-31) and the blanket group arm (`4291b9a5600e`, 2026-07-09) both PREDATE 8fbd; 8fbd's plan enabled the anthropic fallback in rebar.toml, activating both latent defects without a chain-disposition-preserving terminal. Fix site (failure.py/model_classes.py) ≠ cause site (8fbd's config plan).\n\nNext: `rebar review-plan` exit gate, then land via Gerrit."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788054020445953212,"uuid":"573205c9-9043-4384-a6e7-4a89d57f9b84"}